# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space for the latest version of Qiskit bosons"
msgstr "Mensintesis Evolution gate di ruang bosonik untuk Qiskit bosons versi terbaru"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space"
msgstr "Mensintesis Evolution gate di ruang bosonik"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bosonic-synthesis-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space {#synthesize-an-evolution-gate-in-bosonic-space}"
msgstr "Mensintesis Evolution gate di ruang bosonik {#synthesize-an-evolution-gate-in-bosonic-space}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The time evolution $e^{-itH}$ of a Hamiltonian that is a sum of non-commuting pieces cannot be implemented exactly gate by gate. A **product formula** approximates it by a sequence of short evolutions under the individual pieces, and the approximation error is called the Trotter error.\n"
msgstr "Evolusi waktu $e^{-itH}$ dari Hamiltonian yang merupakan jumlah dari bagian-bagian yang tidak komut tidak bisa diimplementasikan secara eksak gate demi gate. **Product formula** memperkirakannya dengan serangkaian evolusi singkat di bawah masing-masing bagian, dan error aproksimasinya disebut error Trotter.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can apply a product formula in two places, and they are not interchangeable:\n"
msgstr "Kamu bisa menerapkan product formula di dua tempat, dan keduanya tidak bisa saling menggantikan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**In bosonic space**, before any truncation or encoding has been chosen. The formula sees the *groups* of the operator (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)) and can interleave them.\n"
msgstr "**Di ruang bosonik**, sebelum truncation atau encoding dipilih. Formula ini melihat *grup* dari operator (lihat [Mengelompokkan suku operator: manfaatkan struktur operator](grouping#grouping-explanation)) dan bisa menyisipkannya secara berselang-seling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**In qubit space**, inside Qiskit’s [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), after the operator has been mapped. The formula sees one Pauli operator per group and can only subdivide the terms *within* it.\n"
msgstr "**Di ruang qubit**, di dalam [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) milik Qiskit, setelah operator dipetakan. Formula ini melihat satu operator Pauli per grup dan hanya bisa membagi suku-suku *di dalamnya*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only the first can reduce the error between groups that do not commute, which is usually the dominant one. This guide shows how to use it.\n"
msgstr "Hanya yang pertama yang bisa mengurangi error antar grup yang tidak komut, yang biasanya paling dominan. Panduan ini menunjukkan cara memakainya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Both steps are optional. An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate that is never decomposed in bosonic space reaches the boson-to-qubit stage whole and is mapped and synthesized there. That incurs *no* error at the bosonic level, only whatever the qubit-level formula introduces.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Kedua langkah ini opsional. Sebuah gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") yang tidak pernah didekomposisi di ruang bosonik sampai ke tahap boson-ke-qubit secara utuh, lalu dipetakan dan disintesis di sana. Itu *tidak* menimbulkan error di level bosonik, hanya apa pun yang diperkenalkan formula level qubit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up {#set-up}"
msgstr "Persiapan {#set-up}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A two-site Bose-Hubbard chain, the smallest example in which the groups do not commute (see [Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) for the full model). It is grouped into one Hermitian group for the bond and one diagonal group for the on-site interaction:\n"
msgstr "Rantai Bose-Hubbard dua situs, contoh terkecil di mana grup-grupnya tidak komut (lihat [Simulasi dinamika Bose-Hubbard dengan pilihan encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) untuk model lengkapnya). Rantai ini dikelompokkan menjadi satu grup Hermitian untuk bond dan satu grup diagonal untuk interaksi on-site:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To measure an error you need a reference. The exact evolution of the Hamiltonian *as mapped at the same truncation* is the right one, because the truncation is a separate approximation:\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengukur error, kamu butuh referensi. Evolusi eksak dari Hamiltonian *yang dipetakan pada truncation yang sama* adalah pilihan yang tepat, karena truncation adalah aproksimasi yang terpisah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `error` deliberately simulates the lowered circuit *without* decomposing its [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) instances. [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) applies each as the exact exponential of its group, so the only thing left is the product of group exponentials that the bosonic synthesis chose.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `error` sengaja mensimulasikan circuit hasil lowering *tanpa* mendekomposisi instance [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)-nya. [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) menerapkan masing-masing sebagai eksponensial eksak dari grupnya, jadi satu-satunya yang tersisa adalah hasil kali eksponensial grup yang dipilih oleh sintesis bosonik.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The default {#the-default}"
msgstr "Default {#the-default}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With no `synthesis` argument an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate decomposes with [`BosonicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-lie-trotter#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter\"), the first-order formula: one factor per group, each for the whole time.\n"
msgstr "Tanpa argumen `synthesis`, gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") didekomposisi dengan [`BosonicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-lie-trotter#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter\"), formula orde pertama: satu faktor per grup, masing-masing untuk seluruh waktu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Without decomposing, the whole gate is handed to the qubit stage and there is no bosonic Trotter error at all:\n"
msgstr "Tanpa dekomposisi, seluruh gate diserahkan ke tahap qubit dan sama sekali tidak ada error Trotter bosonik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Decomposed, a genuine error appears, because the two groups do not commute:\n"
msgstr "Setelah didekomposisi, muncul error yang nyata, karena kedua grup tidak komut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reduce the error {#reduce-the-error}"
msgstr "Kurangi error {#reduce-the-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass a different synthesis method to the gate. A higher **order** composes the factors symmetrically so that the leading error terms cancel; more **repetitions** divide the time into shorter steps.\n"
msgstr "Berikan metode sintesis yang berbeda ke gate. **Orde** yang lebih tinggi menyusun faktor-faktor secara simetris sehingga suku error utamanya saling meniadakan; lebih banyak **repetisi** membagi waktu menjadi langkah-langkah yang lebih pendek.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each increase of the order by two composes five sweeps of the one below (the $5^{(k-2)/2}$ growth of Suzuki’s recursion, applied to the $2n - 1$ factors of order 2), which is the count in the last line, marked with a star. The sweeps meet on the same factor, so the neighboring gates evolve under one operator and are fused into a single gate with the summed time. That saves one gate per seam and is exact. Pass `merge_adjacent=False` to keep the textbook sequence. Either way, a higher order buys a smaller error:\n"
msgstr "Setiap kenaikan orde sebesar dua menyusun lima sapuan dari orde di bawahnya (pertumbuhan $5^{(k-2)/2}$ dari rekursi Suzuki, diterapkan pada $2n - 1$ faktor dari orde 2), yaitu jumlah pada baris terakhir, yang ditandai bintang. Sapuan-sapuan itu bertemu di faktor yang sama, sehingga gate bertetangga berevolusi di bawah satu operator dan digabung menjadi satu gate dengan waktu yang dijumlahkan. Itu menghemat satu gate per sambungan dan bersifat eksak. Berikan `merge_adjacent=False` untuk mempertahankan urutan versi buku teks. Bagaimanapun, orde yang lebih tinggi memberi error yang lebih kecil:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repetitions trade depth for accuracy at a different rate. The first-order error falls linearly in the step size, the second-order one quadratically:\n"
msgstr "Repetisi menukar depth dengan akurasi pada laju yang berbeda. Error orde pertama turun secara linear terhadap ukuran langkah, sedangkan orde kedua secara kuadratik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which is the better trade depends on the operator. Note that an operator with a single group is exact at any order, because a lone factor commutes with itself, and the formula then collapses to one gate rather than re-splitting it.\n"
msgstr "Mana yang lebih baik tergantung pada operatornya. Perhatikan bahwa operator dengan satu grup saja eksak pada orde berapa pun, karena satu faktor tunggal komut dengan dirinya sendiri, dan formula itu lalu menyusut menjadi satu gate alih-alih membaginya ulang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure the cost {#measure-the-cost}"
msgstr "Ukur biayanya {#measure-the-cost}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A smaller error costs more factors, and each factor costs entangling gates once the qubit stage has synthesized it. How many depends on the encoding, so count them through the preset pipeline, with the basis fixed and no qubit-level optimization (`optimization_level=0`), to see the price of each method:\n"
msgstr "Error yang lebih kecil butuh lebih banyak faktor, dan setiap faktor memakan gate entangling setelah tahap qubit mensintesisnya. Berapa banyaknya tergantung pada encoding, jadi hitung lewat pipeline preset, dengan basis tetap dan tanpa optimisasi level qubit (`optimization_level=0`), untuk melihat harga tiap metode:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The exact counts depend on how Qiskit synthesizes the evolution gates, which changes between releases, so the plot shows them rather than a table:\n"
msgstr "Jumlah persisnya bergantung pada cara Qiskit mensintesis evolution gate, yang berubah antar rilis, jadi plot menampilkannya sebagai ganti tabel:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Grouped bar chart of the CX count for Lie-Trotter and Suzuki of order 2 and 4, for the Gray and the unary encoding. The counts grow with the order, and the unary bars are higher.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bosonic_synthesis-10.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Grouped bar chart of the CX count for Lie-Trotter and Suzuki of order 2 and 4, for the Gray and the unary encoding. The counts grow with the order, and the unary bars are higher.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bosonic_synthesis-10.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each group of bars is a method: Lie-Trotter, Suzuki of order 2, and Suzuki of order 4. The order buys accuracy at a price that grows by the factor of the recursion, and the unary encoding pays more than the Gray code for every method because each of its factors maps to more entangling gates. Choose the method for the accuracy that you need and the encoding for the hardware, and keep the two choices apart: the bosonic circuit above never changes.\n"
msgstr "Setiap kelompok batang adalah satu metode: Lie-Trotter, Suzuki orde 2, dan Suzuki orde 4. Orde membeli akurasi dengan harga yang tumbuh sesuai faktor rekursi, dan encoding unary membayar lebih mahal daripada kode Gray untuk setiap metode karena tiap faktornya dipetakan ke lebih banyak gate entangling. Pilih metode sesuai akurasi yang kamu butuhkan dan encoding sesuai hardware, dan pisahkan kedua pilihan itu: circuit bosonik di atas tidak pernah berubah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply one method to a whole circuit {#apply-one-method-to-a-whole-circuit}"
msgstr "Terapkan satu metode ke seluruh circuit {#apply-one-method-to-a-whole-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To set `synthesis` on each gate, you must thread the choice through everything that builds one. The [`B2BSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-b-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis\") pass makes the choice once for a pipeline instead. Its `config` names the method for each type of gate, and it both selects the method and expands the gates:\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengatur `synthesis` pada setiap gate, kamu harus meneruskan pilihan itu ke semua yang membangunnya. Pass [`B2BSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-b-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis\") membuat pilihan itu sekali untuk seluruh pipeline. `config`-nya menamai metode untuk setiap jenis gate, dan pass ini sekaligus memilih metode dan mengekspansi gate:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A method can also be named, with the arguments for its `__init__`, instead of being built: `B2BSynthesis({\"Evolution\": (\"SuzukiTrotter\", (), {\"order\": 2})})`. The available names are those of the [`B2BSynthesisPluginManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-b-2-b-synthesis-plugin-manager#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.B2BSynthesisPluginManager \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.B2BSynthesisPluginManager\"), and a method that is registered nowhere can be handed over as an instance, as above.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah metode juga bisa disebut namanya, dengan argumen untuk `__init__`-nya, alih-alih dibangun: `B2BSynthesis({\"Evolution\": (\"SuzukiTrotter\", (), {\"order\": 2})})`. Nama yang tersedia adalah milik [`B2BSynthesisPluginManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-b-2-b-synthesis-plugin-manager#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.B2BSynthesisPluginManager \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.B2BSynthesisPluginManager\"), dan metode yang tidak terdaftar di mana pun bisa diserahkan sebagai instance, seperti di atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `apply=False` the pass only selects the method and leaves the expansion to the point where it is wanted, for example to inspect the circuit first. An atomic gate is never touched, not even tagged:\n"
msgstr "Dengan `apply=False`, pass hanya memilih metode dan menunda ekspansi sampai saat dibutuhkan, misalnya untuk memeriksa circuit terlebih dahulu. Gate atomik tidak pernah disentuh, bahkan tidak diberi tag:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An unexpanded gate reaches the boson-to-qubit stage whole, where it is mapped without its `synthesis` being consulted, so every method then produces identical output.\n"
msgstr "Gate yang belum diekspansi sampai ke tahap boson-ke-qubit secara utuh, di mana ia dipetakan tanpa `synthesis`-nya dipertimbangkan, sehingga setiap metode menghasilkan output yang identik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An optional `filter` restricts it to the gates that benefit. Evolutions whose groups all commute, such as a Hamiltonian made only of number operators, are synthesized exactly at any order, so a higher order would only add depth there.\n"
msgstr "`filter` opsional membatasinya pada gate yang diuntungkan. Evolusi yang semua grupnya komut, seperti Hamiltonian yang hanya terdiri dari operator bilangan, disintesis secara eksak pada orde berapa pun, jadi orde yang lebih tinggi hanya menambah depth di sana.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restrict the pass to the gates that benefit {#restrict-the-pass-to-the-gates-that-benefit}"
msgstr "Batasi pass pada gate yang diuntungkan {#restrict-the-pass-to-the-gates-that-benefit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A purely diagonal operator makes the point concrete, because number operators commute with each other. Its groups are exact at first order, and the second order spends entangling gates for nothing:\n"
msgstr "Operator yang murni diagonal membuat poin ini konkret, karena operator bilangan saling komut. Grup-grupnya eksak pada orde pertama, dan orde kedua menghabiskan gate entangling tanpa guna:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both circuits are exact, so the second spends more entangling gates for no gain. (The symmetric order-two formula applies the first group twice at half the time each, and thus the cost depends on which group comes first.) The `filter` takes a predicate over the [`DAGOpNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGOpNode) and leaves the rejected gates untouched, so one pass can raise the order on the gates that benefit and keep the rest at first order. The predicate below accepts a gate only when its operator moves bosons between modes, which is when the groups fail to commute:\n"
msgstr "Kedua circuit eksak, jadi yang kedua memakai lebih banyak gate entangling tanpa keuntungan. (Formula simetris orde dua menerapkan grup pertama dua kali dengan setengah waktu masing-masing, sehingga biayanya bergantung pada grup mana yang datang lebih dulu.) `filter` menerima predikat atas [`DAGOpNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGOpNode) dan membiarkan gate yang ditolak tidak tersentuh, sehingga satu pass bisa menaikkan orde pada gate yang diuntungkan dan mempertahankan sisanya di orde pertama. Predikat di bawah menerima gate hanya jika operatornya memindahkan boson antar mode, yaitu saat grup-grupnya tidak komut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you run the pass again, nothing changes: the factors it emits are *atomic*.\n"
msgstr "Kalau kamu menjalankan pass itu lagi, tidak ada yang berubah: faktor yang dihasilkannya bersifat *atomik*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Atomic factors {#atomic-factors}"
msgstr "Faktor atomik {#atomic-factors}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") marked `atomic` has no definition, so [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose\") leaves it in place however often it is applied. A synthesis marks the factors it emits this way, and so does [`BosonicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-q-drift#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicQDrift \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicQDrift\") for the terms it samples.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") yang ditandai `atomic` tidak punya definisi, sehingga [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose\") membiarkannya di tempat sebanyak apa pun ia diterapkan. Sebuah sintesis menandai faktor yang dihasilkannya dengan cara ini, begitu pula [`BosonicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-q-drift#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicQDrift \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicQDrift\") untuk suku yang disampelnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is more than tidiness. Splitting a Hermitian group further, term by term, yields factors that are individually **not** Hermitian, and the exponential of a non-Hermitian operator is not unitary:\n"
msgstr "Ini lebih dari sekadar kerapian. Membagi grup Hermitian lebih lanjut, suku demi suku, menghasilkan faktor yang masing-masing **tidak** Hermitian, dan eksponensial dari operator non-Hermitian tidak unitari:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Caution\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Each factor must be Hermitian on its own. A Hermitian operator split into groups can produce non-Hermitian ones, such as a hopping term separated from its adjoint. Check with [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\"). An operator *without* groups is split term by term, and the qubit stage then rejects the factors with `Operator contains complex coefficients`. The symmetrization of an even order partially cancels the error of a non-Hermitian factor, so a wrongly grouped operator can look better at order 2 than at order 1 while still being wrong.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Perhatian\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Setiap faktor harus Hermitian dengan sendirinya. Operator Hermitian yang dibagi menjadi grup bisa menghasilkan grup non-Hermitian, seperti suku hopping yang dipisahkan dari adjoint-nya. Periksa dengan [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\"). Operator *tanpa* grup dibagi suku demi suku, dan tahap qubit lalu menolak faktornya dengan `Operator contains complex coefficients`. Simetrisasi pada orde genap sebagian meniadakan error dari faktor non-Hermitian, sehingga operator yang pengelompokannya salah bisa tampak lebih baik pada orde 2 daripada orde 1 padahal tetap salah.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat a short step {#repeat-a-short-step}"
msgstr "Ulangi langkah pendek {#repeat-a-short-step}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a circuit-level alternative, build one short Trotter step and repeat it. [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat\") flattens the repetitions into one circuit and leaves the boundaries adjacent, so passes can act across them:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai alternatif di level circuit, bangun satu langkah Trotter pendek lalu ulangi. [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat\") meratakan repetisi menjadi satu circuit dan membiarkan batasnya bersebelahan, sehingga pass bisa bekerja melintasinya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass `insert_barriers=True` to keep the repetitions apart. A barrier is mapped onto every qubit of the registers it touches, because an encoding needs several qubits per mode and a mode has no per-qubit image of its own:\n"
msgstr "Berikan `insert_barriers=True` untuk memisahkan repetisi. Barrier dipetakan ke setiap qubit dari register yang disentuhnya, karena sebuah encoding butuh beberapa qubit per mode dan mode tidak punya citra per qubit sendiri:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `repeat` is unrelated to the `reps` of a synthesis method. A synthesis subdivides a *single* evolution into more, shorter factors. Repeating a circuit that holds one evolution merely multiplies its total time.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `repeat` tidak berkaitan dengan `reps` pada metode sintesis. Sebuah sintesis membagi *satu* evolusi menjadi lebih banyak faktor yang lebih pendek. Mengulang circuit yang berisi satu evolusi hanya melipatgandakan total waktunya.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combine with a qubit-level formula {#combine-with-a-qubit-level-formula}"
msgstr "Gabungkan dengan formula level qubit {#combine-with-a-qubit-level-formula}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two levels compose, and where both approximate, the accuracy of the result is governed by the weaker of the two. Raising the bosonic order while the qubit-side formula stays first-order buys little. See `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` for the qubit-side formula. It keeps the Pauli term order that the mapper chose, and so `group_wise()` can emit the terms of each group adjacent to one another, and `simplify()` can pin a canonical order instead.\n"
msgstr "Kedua level ini bisa dikomposisikan, dan jika keduanya mengaproksimasi, akurasi hasil ditentukan oleh yang lebih lemah. Menaikkan orde bosonik sementara formula sisi qubit tetap orde pertama tidak banyak membantu. Lihat `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` untuk formula sisi qubit. Ia mempertahankan urutan suku Pauli yang dipilih mapper, sehingga `group_wise()` bisa mengeluarkan suku-suku tiap grup secara bersebelahan, dan `simplify()` bisa mengunci urutan kanonik sebagai gantinya.\n"

